    {
      "id": "3752b13d-8b2f-48a1-98c9-95408f78c0f7",
      "phaseId": "5de43f15-8304-4f64-870f-8514d534d5a5",
      "number": 352,
      "shortId": "VKF85",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "focus-is-the-mode-route-the-ke",
      "title": "Focus is the mode: route the keyboard to the focused component",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "# What\n\nMake chrome focus decide where unprefixed keys go. No `InputMode` variant: focus is already the fact,\nand a mode beside it would be a second one that can disagree.\n\n# Current state\n\n`handle_keyboard_input` (`heca/src/app/input.rs:34`): `InputMode::Normal` forwards every unbound key to\nthe focused pane's backend (`:58-88`) after trying the `global` keymap. Prefix mode\n(`handle_prefix_mode`, `:208`) resolves mode triggers, then the `normal` map, then **drops** the key\n(`:275` — the `else if !ctx.key_text.is_empty()` arm just exits prefix). `InputMode::SidebarNav` is a\nbespoke arm delegating to the `\"sidebar\"` mode keymap (`handle_sidebar_nav_mode`, `:584`).\n\n# ✅ DECIDED — the order, in every focus state\n\n1. prefix key → prefix mode → mode triggers → global `normal` map → **falls through to the focused\n   component's `[keys.<kind>]` layer** (user decision 2026-07-29) → drop\n2. global direct bindings (`Alt+Enter`, `Shift+PageUp`, …) — unchanged\n3. **if a component holds chrome focus** → its layer → **swallow** if unbound (user decision: a `j`\n   leaking into a shell is the worse failure)\n4. otherwise → forward to the focused pane's backend, as today\n\n`state.focused_pane` is **not** cleared: chrome focus redirects the keyboard, nothing else, so\n`prefix+Enter` still splits the pane you last worked in.\n\n# Steps\n\n1. One branch at the top of the `InputMode::Normal` arm: chrome focus set ⇒ resolve in the component\n   layer, else the existing terminal-forward path. Unbound ⇒ consume (do not forward).\n2. Prefix fall-through: after the `normal` map misses, try the focused component's layer before\n   dropping.\n3. Suppress the **double-prefix literal forward** (`prefix_combo_to_literal_input`, `input.rs:224`)\n   while a component has focus — nothing there is receiving text, so sending a literal `Ctrl+B` to a\n   pane the user is not typing in is a surprise.\n4. `Esc` returns focus to the pane (clear `focused_container`); `focus_dock` aimed at the\n   already-focused dock toggles focus back off.\n5. Keyboard scrolling — **this is all that is left of F003/P011/T012**: the existing\n   `ScrollPageUp/Down/ToTop/ToBottom` (+ line variants) handlers gain one branch — chrome focus set ⇒\n   send the matching `Event::Widget(WidgetIntent::Scroll*)` into the chrome tree (the FocusScope\n   delivers it to the focused container, everything else is inert); else the terminal viewport path,\n   unchanged. Add the four horizontal actions. **This supersedes T012's prefix-gated route**: with\n   focus as the mode, plain `PageUp/PageDown/Home/End` are free while a dock is focused (nothing is\n   being forwarded), and the `Shift+` variants stay as they are for the pane case.\n6. A **declined** intent (`Handled::No` — e.g. a container with nothing scrollable) stops at the\n   chrome; it does **not** fall through to the pane. The nesting rule is about nested *scroll areas*,\n   and the pane is not an outer scroll area of the sidebar.\n7. Status bar: derive the mode word from the focused component's `title()` (`status_mode_parts`,\n   `app/render.rs:54`) so unprefixed keys never go somewhere invisible. The focus ring is the other\n   half of that guardrail.\n\n# Edge cases\n\n- Prefix, hint pick, and every mode trigger must keep working while a component is focused (they are\n  resolved first, by construction).\n- A pick mode (`DockPick`, `PaneSelect`, …) is entered *from* a focused component and must still\n  resolve normally.\n- Nothing may reach a backend while chrome focus is set — audit every `process_input` call on the\n  Normal path.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- With a dock focused: its keys work unprefixed, `prefix+…` still works, unbound keys do nothing, and\n  nothing reaches the terminal.\n- `PageUp`/`PageDown`/`Home`/`End` scroll the focused dock; the same keys with `Shift` still scroll the\n  focused pane when no dock is focused.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings. **The USER drives it in the app** — this is interaction.",
      "notes": "",
